QuestGuidance.Register("en",439,{
[14017]="70064478\n1\tReturn to your spawning den. Speak with Zagfra the Corruptor.\tMalavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Zagfra the Corruptor.\n",
[14018]="7007035E\n1\tTalk to Cinaid\tMalavin directed you to return to Cinaid near the front gate of Gramsfoot. He will aid you further in preparing to battle throughout the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14019]="7002612F\n1\tGet your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz\tTolothdal has ordered you to get into the fight already. She wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.\n2\tReturn to safety and speak with Uglash\tYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the camp to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14020]="700261DC\n1\tGet your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz\tTolothdal has ordered you to get into the fight already. She wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.\n2\tReturn to safety and speak with Uglash\tYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14021]="70064481\n1\tArrive at the keep of Dâr-gazag\tLeave Gramsfoot by way of the hidden path along the mountainside to the west. Or, if you are feeling adventurous wander outside the main gate of Gramsfoot, but beware, the Freeps can attack you if you do not take the mountainside path. Your goal is to reach the keep, Dâr-gazag.\n2\tUse the skill Return to Gramsfoot to return\tYou reached Dâr-gazag and should now return to Gramsfoot to complete your training.\n3\tSpeak with Uglash\tNow that you have returned to Gramsfoot, speak with Uglash, the task-master.\n",
[14022]="7001B9D9\n1\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is at his camp just outside of Bree's South-gate. He is waiting for you to report in.\n2\tUse the horn to learn how to call a Soldier\tThe horn is on a crate next to Second-watcher Heathstraw. You will need to use it in order to learn how to call forth a Soldier into the battle.\n3\tUse your new skill to call forth a Soldier\tThe Soldier skill is in your Skill Panel under the Skirmish section. You will need to use this skill to summon a Soldier to aid you.\n4\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is at his camp just outside the South-gate of Bree. He wishes to discuss his plan for retaking the town with you.\n5\tTake control of Bree's South-gate\tThe South-gate is just north of Second-watcher Heathstraw's camp. You will need to clear all of the enemies from around the banner in order to claim it.\n6\tUse the banner to claim the South-gate\tThe banner is at the South-gate of Bree. In order to claim this Control Point you need to use the banner.\n7\tTake control of Bree's Auction House\tThe Auction House is north of the South-gate of Bree. The enemies must be cleared and the banner used to take this point.\n8\tTake control of Bill Ferny's house and defeat Dríthlorz\tBill Ferny's house is east of the Auction House. Dríthlorz and his allies must be defeated and the banner used in order to reclaim this part of Bree.\n9\tReport your success to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside of Bill Ferny's house. He wishes to discuss your victory with you.\n",
[14023]="700260BF\n1\tGet your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz\tMorsûm has ordered you to get into the fight already. He wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.\n2\tReturn to safety and speak with Uglash\tYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14024]="700261DD\n1\tGet your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz\tMorsûm has ordered you to get into the fight already. He wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.\n2\tReturn to safety and speak with Uglash\tYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14025]="70026130\n1\tGet your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz\tSoldier Gazfríb has ordered you to get into the fight already. He wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.\n2\tReturn to safety and talk to Uglash\tYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the fort to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14026]="700261DE\n1\tGet your orders from Chief Guard Duthúrz\tSoldier Gazfríb has ordered you to get into the fight already. He wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.\n2\tReturn to safety and speak with Uglash\tYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Moors.\n",
[14027]="700261AC\n1\tReturn to your trainers and learn how to train your skills\tUglash has asked you to return to your trainers and learn more about what it takes to become a true soldier in the war against the Free Peoples. The trainers are back where you started your life as a spider. Speak with Lingemil first.\n2\tTalk to Lenathron, a Corruptor of Gramsfoot\tHaving spoken with Lingemil, you should now talk to the Corruptor to learn about traits.\n3\tTalk to Nathrog\tNow that you have equipped some Traits, speak with Nathrog to learn more about Corruptions in Monster Play.\n4\tTalk to Uglash to finish the tutorial\tNow that you have learned how to best equip yourself in Monster Play, speak with Uglash again for final instructions.\n",
[14028]="70054677\n1\tScout northern fortifications to the west of Barad Angarth\030Scout central fortifications to the west of Barad Angarth\030Scout southern fortifications to the west of Barad Angarth\tAn army has begun to fortify the area west of Barad Angarth. Scout several locations within the camp and you may gain additional information about your foe.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol\tDolenthol awaits your findings in the field. You should locate the Ranger and make your report.\n",
[14029]="7002D457\n1\tBring bag of turtles to Sig Mandrake at his shop\tSig Mandrake is in his shop east of the Mud-gate, in the village of Bree, located in the south-western section of the town. Grobo Dogwort wants you to bring the bag of turtles to Sig Mandrake and to ask the shop-keeper for any news of Grobo's nephew.\n2\tFind Benegar Longbottom and talk to him among the Everclear Lakes\tBenegar Longbottom went to an island in the Everclear Lakes, north-west of Bree, to look for turtles to provide Sig Mandrake. You have learned where Benegar Longbottom went and should look for him to make sure he is safe.\n",
[14030]="70026F3A\n1\tCollect stolen food-stores from the Dragon-clan scouts (total: 8)\tStolen food and supplies can surely be found on the Dragon-clan scouts who invaded the farm. You should steal food-stores back from them and bring them to the starving huddle of outcasts.\n2\tBring the stolen food to the hiding Dunlendings\tCeri, the leader of the small band of frightened outcasts, is at their tiny camp on the overlook just north-west of the herd-lands. You should return to Ceri whith the stolen goods you have collected so that his folk may survive their journey through these harsh lands.\n",
[14031]="7005A536\n1\tPoisoned warriors are resting in Amdân. Edash has tasked you with administering an antidote to the poisoned warriors.\t\n2\tTalk to Edash\tEdash is located in Amdân. Bring the antidote pouch to Edash.\n",
[14032]="7003E44D\n1\tDefeat wood-trolls in Fangorn Forest (total: 10)\tWood-trolls can be found in north-western Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam's Huorn seeks to drive the cruel wood-trolls from the forest, and would benefit from your aid.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam's Huorn\tYou have defeated many wood-trolls, freeing the forest from their vile influence.\n",
[14033]="70026195\n1\tAid Erchiel at The Twisted Grove\030Aid Lithuifin in The Twisted Grove\030Aid Remmenylf in The Twisted Grove\tThe Elves of the Eavespires have some plans for the Twisted Grove.\n2\tTalk to Longbough at the Eavespires\tLongbough is at the Eavespires. Longbough will want to hear that the evil at the Twisted Grove is more powerful than previously thought.\n",
[14034]="700606FB\n1\tTalk to Glatharn\tGlatharn is located in Tham Lumren. Thalathril has suggested you offer your assistance to Glatharn.\n2\tCollect twisted armbands (total: 12)\tTwisted spirits can be found at Tham Lumren, in the north-east Angle. Glatharn has asked you to collect twisted armbands from twisted spirits.\n3\tReturn to Glatharn\tGlatharn is located in Tham Lumren. You should bring the twisted armbands to Glatharn.\n4\tCollect twisted rotroot (total: 6)\tTwisted rotroot can be found along the banks of the rivers that border the Angle. Glatharn has asked you to collect a bouquet of twisted rotroot.\n5\tReturn to Glatharn\tGlatharn is located in Tham Lumren. You should bring the twisted rotroot flowers to Glatharn.\n6\tAdd the armbands and bouquet to the pyre\tThe pyre is in Tham Lumren, in the eastern Angle. Glatharn has asked you to add the twisted rotroot and armbands to the pyre.\n7\tReturn to Glatharn\tGlatharn is located in Tham Lumren. You should talk to Glatharn.\n",
[14035]="700454FC\n1\tDefeat spiders in Taur Drúadan (total: 10)\tSpiders can be found in the woods of Taur Drúadan. You should defeat spiders in Taur Drúadan.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many spiders in Taur Drúadan.\n",
[14036]="700077E4\n1\tDefeat Gurzstâz\030Defeat Gurzrum\tThe two chieftains, Gurzstâz and Gurzrum, are likely to be found in the Goblinhole Ruins in the southern stretch of the Midgewater Marshes. Bill Mossfoot believes that slaying the goblin-chieftains will drive the rest away.\n2\tTalk to Bill Mossfoot\tBill Mossfoot is at the camp in the Midgewater Marsh, south-east of the Midgewater Ruins. Bill Mossfoot will be pleased to hear of your success with the two goblin-chieftans he asked you to dispatch.\n3\tTalk to Watcher Redweed in Staddle\tWatcher Redweed is in Staddle town centre. The defeat of the goblin-chieftains in the Midgewater Marshes should be a great relief to Watcher Redweed.\n",
[14037]="7001750D\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the Water-works (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found in the Water-works, east and north-east of the Great Wheel. Foreman Indrith wants to best two problems with one foray. If the Orcs in the Water-works are afraid of anything, they may mention it as they fight.\n2\tTalk to Foreman Indrith in the Chamber of Wheels\tForeman Indrith is in the Chamber of Wheels, beneath the Great Wheel. While ridding the Water-works of the Orcs, a few of the creatures did mention that they were afraid of tentacles dragging them down into the cold water.\n",
[14038]="70060586\n1\tFind the spies' base in Thelgarth\tThelgarth lies to the south of the Cuan-lûth Refuge. You should find the spies' base in Thelgarth.\n2\tTalk to Cariad\tCariad would like to speak with you.\n3\tDestroy the spy reports\tYou should destroy the spy reports.\n4\tTalk to Cariad\tYou should discuss the next course of action with Cariad.\n",
[14039]="7006139B\n1\tTalk to Ramsa Twelling\tRamsa Twelling can be found in Gamwich. Adamanda North-took has asked you to bring the rope to Ramsa Twelling and have her weave it into a net.\n2\tCollect honey\tFresh honey can be found in hives near Ramsa's dwelling in Gamwich. Ramsa Twelling has asked you to collect honey from her hives.\n3\tBring the honey to Pello\tPello can be found in the Brimful Quiver, in Gamwich. You should bring the honey to Pello Hartstongue and exchange it for a bottle of mead.\n4\tCollect the bottle of mead\tThe bottle of mead can be found in the Brimful Quiver, in Gamwich. Pello has given you permission to collect a bottle of mead from the back room.\n5\tReturn to Ramsa\tRamsa is in Gamwich. You should bring the mead to Ramsa Twelling.\n6\tAdd knots to the net (0/80)\tThe net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich. Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.\n7\tAdd knots to the net (1/80)\tThe net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich. Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.\n8\tAdd knots to the net (2/80)\tThe net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich. Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.\n9\tAdd knots to the net (3/80)\tThe net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich. Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.\n10\tTalk to Ramsa\tRamsa is in Gamwich. You should talk to Ramsa.\n11\tCollect the completed net\tThe net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich. You should collect the net and bring it to Adamanda.\n12\tBring the net to Adamanda\tAdamanda North-took can be found near Nobottle. You should bring the net to Adamanda.\n",
[14040]="70060018\n1\tDefeat foes at Tâg Fógarrach\tTâg Fógarrach can be found in western Câr Bronach. You should defeat foes at Tâg Fógarrach.\n2\tDefeat foes at Tâg Fógarrach (total: 10)\tTâg Fógarrach can be found in western Câr Bronach. You should defeat foes at Tâg Fógarrach.\n",
[14041]="70015E03\n1\tAkashpug is at Târ Stazg, north-east of Echad Dúnann, along the mountains before the Redhorn Gate. Palanaer has instructed you to call forth Akashpug with the horn and defeat him.\t\n2\tTalk to Palanaer\tPalanaer is in Echad Dúnann, south-west of Târ Stazg. You should return to Palanaer with news of Akashpug's defeat.\n",
[14042]="70040104\n1\tCollect the treasure-map (quantity: see journal)\030Collect the stick-sword (quantity: see journal)\030Collect small rocks to use as play-treasure (total: 6)\tTúmir's treasure-map and stick-sword can be found in his bedroom. The small stones can be collected outside the house. You should collect everything Túmir asked for.\n2\tBring the toys and treasure map to Túmir\tTúmir is in his father's home in northern Lamedon. You should bring everything you gathered to Túmir.\n3\tBring Túmir's gift to Fuirion\tFuirion is in Gladion's home in northern Lamedon. You should bring Túmir's gift to Fuirion.\n",
[14043]="7006D324\n1\tDefeat the Pahór-korat, the Hands of Forgetting\tExplore the marketplace of the Tûl Zakana, the Well of Forgetting.\n2\tDefeat Mûkh Bahora, the Mouth of Forgetting\tBahádring's path leads you deeper into Tûl Zakana. Steel yourself for the dangers to come and press further into the Well of Forgetting.\n3\tDefeat Bahádring the Unmindful\tBahádring has run off again. You must be close to the Well itself. Can it really make you forget everything?\n",
[14044]="7006D327\n1\tDefeat the Pahór-korat, the Hands of Forgetting\tExplore the marketplace of the Tûl Zakana, the Well of Forgetting.\n2\tDefeat Mûkh Bahora, the Mouth of Forgetting\tBahádring's path leads you deeper into Tûl Zakana. Steel yourself for the dangers to come and press further into the Well of Forgetting.\n3\tDefeat Bahádring the Unmindful\tBahádring has run off again. You must be close to the Well itself. Can it really make you forget everything?\n",
